<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Joaquín Pérez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1801">1801</a>–<a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Joaquín Pérez was president of Chile from 1861 to 1871, the last of the four presidents who each served two consecutive five-year terms. A moderate conservative, he governed through broad coalitions and eased the conflicts left by the Montt era. His presidency saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chincha-islands-war">Chincha Islands War</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and advances into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> lands in Araucanía.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-joaquin-perez.jpg" alt="José Joaquín Pérez" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Joaqu%C3%ADn_Perez.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
